\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n| $1$ | $2$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 2.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the second row) and new values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}={2}^{2}-{1}^{2}=3 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=3\\cdot 1=3 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=1+1=2 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=2+3=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n| $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $3$ |\n| $2$ | $5$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 3.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the third row) and new values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}={5}^{2}-{2}^{2}=21 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=21\\cdot 1=21 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=2+1=3 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=5+21=26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n| $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $3$ |\n| $2$ | $5$ | $21$ | $21$ |\n| $3$ | $26$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(3)≈26.$" 13194139535488 true] [17592186351667 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351668 13194139535488 true] [17592186351667 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351669 13194139535488 true] [17592186351667 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351670 13194139535488 true] [17592186351667 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351671 13194139535488 true] [17592186351667 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351672 13194139535488 true] [17592186351667 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535488 true] [17592186351667 1041 "selection" 13194139535488 true] [17592186351667 1104 #edb/ref 17592186351669 13194139535488 true] [17592186351667 1110 #uuid "5f04d5f3-56b7-568c-9133-da2970e11975" 13194139535488 true] [17592186351668 1034 "28" 13194139535488 true] [17592186351668 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 131941